WEBVTT

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.319
welcome to this tutorial from the ncvs

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:07.020
I'm Brad story a professor in the

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.400
department of speech language and

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.920
hearing sciences at the University of

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.099
Arizona

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.279
this tutorial is a brief explanation of

00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:19.500
vocal tract resonances and their

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.779
Associated standing waves specifically

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:25.460
as they relate to vowel production

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:29.279
typical production of vowels is based on

00:00:29.279 --> 00:00:31.740
vibration of the vocal folds providing a

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.719
Sound Source that is filtered by the

00:00:33.719 --> 00:00:35.640
acoustic characteristics of the vocal

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.780
tract

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.579
the sound that radiates at the lip

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:41.399
opening contains information of both the

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:44.360
source and filter

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.520
an example spectrum of a voice Source

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.920
signal is shown here it contains a

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.200
fundamental frequency component and many

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.199
harmonics whose amplitudes decrease as a

00:00:55.199 --> 00:00:58.699
function of increasing frequency

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.160
an example spectrum of the output

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.140
pressure at the lip opening is shown

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.780
here it contains exactly the same

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.000
fundamental frequency component and

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.340
harmonics except that their amplitudes

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.320
have been modified by the filtering

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.760
effect of the vocal tract

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:20.460
a spectral envelope is a curve that

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.860
encompasses the amplitudes of the

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:24.960
harmonics in a spectrum

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.000
a spectral envelope has been constructed

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.340
for both The Source spectrum and output

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.840
Spectrum

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.759
The Source spectral envelope indicates

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:35.460
the decrease in harmonic amplitudes as

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:38.159
frequency increases whereas the envelope

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:40.500
of the output Spectrum clearly shows

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.420
distinct regions or Peaks where the

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.460
harmonic energy has been enhanced

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.579
relative to other regions

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:49.799
these regions of the spectrum

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:52.079
with enhanced energy are called formants

00:01:52.079 --> 00:01:54.840
or formant frequencies and result from

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.880
the acoustic effect of the vocal tract

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.380
on the source Spectrum

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.899
to better understand how the vocal tract

00:02:03.899 --> 00:02:06.780
enhances the source Spectrum it is often

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.300
easiest to begin by imagining the vocal

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.180
tract to be a simple tube of uniform

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.700
cross-section extending from the vocal

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.900
folds to the lips

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.940
the tube is considered to be closed at

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.459
the end closest to the larynx and open

00:02:23.459 --> 00:02:24.959
at the lips

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:27.360
the vibration of the vocal folds does

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.400
open and close the glottis that is the

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.800
airspace between the vocal folds at the

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.080
closed end to inject sound into the

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.580
vocal tract

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.620
the size of the glottal opening however

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.660
is small compared to the cross section

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.120
of the vocal tract and there is

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.280
potentially much time during each vocal

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.160
fold vibratory cycle that the glottis is

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.959
actually closed

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:51.060
both of these conditions motivate the

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.819
use of a closed open tube as a model of

00:02:53.819 --> 00:02:56.640
the vocal tract

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.819
note also that the nearly 90 degree Bend

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:02.099
in an actual vocal tract is not

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.680
represented by the uniform tube

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.660
although the band is biomechanically

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.400
significant for providing an efficient

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.560
means of deforming the tube shape during

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.200
speech it is a much less significance

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.640
from an acoustic perspective

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.019
the average vocal tract length for an

00:03:19.019 --> 00:03:21.000
adult male is about 17 and a half

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.500
centimeters

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.659
a closed open uniform tube of this

00:03:24.659 --> 00:03:26.400
specific length can be characterized

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:29.099
acoustically by the frequency response

00:03:29.099 --> 00:03:31.140
function shown here

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.120
the frequency response function or

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:35.819
sometimes called a transfer function is

00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:38.700
not a spectrum of a particular sound but

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.739
rather indicates the effect that the

00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:43.080
uniform tube would have on any frequency

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.659
component of a sound propagating through

00:03:45.659 --> 00:03:47.900
it

00:03:48.959 --> 00:03:50.700
the peaks in the frequency response

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.400
function correspond to the resonances or

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.560
natural frequencies of the particular

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.140
tube configuration and they can be

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.879
considered the origin of the formant

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:02.940
frequencies that is the resonances of

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:05.220
the vocal tract enhance the amplitudes

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:09.500
of particular regions of frequencies

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.459
when a sinusoidal wave with a frequency

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:16.560
matched to the first Resonance of the

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.799
uniform tube is injected through a tiny

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:22.199
aperture at the closed end a standing

00:04:22.199 --> 00:04:24.600
wave is produced within the tube that

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.979
extends along its length

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.259
in the case shown here the frequency of

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:34.560
the input sinusoid is 500 Hertz the same

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.500
frequency as the first tube resonance

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.360
the acoustic pressure along the tube

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.300
length is shown as a variation in color

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.880
the deepest red indicates large positive

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.460
pressure the deepest blue indicates

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.259
large negative pressure

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:51.960
and light green represents zero or

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.940
atmospheric pressure

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.040
the plot just above the tube also

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.440
indicates pressure along the tube length

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.000
but is shown as a traditional

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.280
two-dimensional plot of pressure versus

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.300
distance from the closed end or glottis

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.520
although the input frequency is 500

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.580
Hertz the animation is shown in extreme

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.440
slow motion so that the pressure

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.479
variations can be visually trapped

00:05:17.699 --> 00:05:19.440
note that the pressure oscillates

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.960
between large positive values to large

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.020
negative values at the closed end and

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.720
tapers to zero at the open end

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.699
that is the closed end provides

00:05:29.699 --> 00:05:31.919
containment of the error and allows for

00:05:31.919 --> 00:05:34.259
a buildup of pressure whereas at the

00:05:34.259 --> 00:05:36.479
open end the pressure must become equal

00:05:36.479 --> 00:05:39.000
to the atmospheric pressure which is

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.860
zero

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.780
these are known as boundary conditions

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.699
that determine the pattern of pressure

00:05:44.699 --> 00:05:48.000
variation that can be reinforced by the

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.160
specific configuration of the tube

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:55.919
when the input frequency is aligned with

00:05:55.919 --> 00:05:58.020
the first Resonance of a closed open

00:05:58.020 --> 00:06:01.199
tube the standing wave produced is one

00:06:01.199 --> 00:06:03.600
quarter of the wavelength

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.300
for this reason closed open tubes are

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.300
sometimes referred to as a quarter wave

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:13.759
resonator or a quarter wave tube

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:19.139
in this case a sinusoidal wave with a

00:06:19.139 --> 00:06:20.400
frequency matched to the second

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.740
Resonance of the uniform tube is

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.020
injected at the closed end again

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:28.699
producing a standing wave

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:31.560
this time however the pattern is

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.539
different there are now two regions

00:06:33.539 --> 00:06:35.580
along the vocal tract length at which

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.380
the pressure oscillates between large

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.319
positive and negative pressures and two

00:06:40.319 --> 00:06:42.840
regions at which the pressure remains at

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.280
zero

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.620
the regions with zero pressure are

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:48.720
located one-third of the length of the

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.100
tube

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.319
and also at the lips

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:54.360
even though the pattern is different the

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:55.979
boundary conditions at the closed and

00:06:55.979 --> 00:06:58.500
open ends of the tube are met just as in

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.120
the previous animation

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.400
in this case three quarters of the

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.259
wavelength comprise the standing wave

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.319
in this case a sinusoidal wave with a

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:15.240
frequency matched to the third Resonance

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.819
of the uniform tube is injected at the

00:07:17.819 --> 00:07:20.460
closed end producing a standing wave

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:25.220
with three zero pressure nodes

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.660
the pattern of pressure is different

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:31.020
than the two previous animations but

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.639
again the boundary conditions at the

00:07:32.639 --> 00:07:37.639
closed and open ends of the tube are met

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.900
for comparison to the previous standing

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.660
wave animations the sinusoidal wave

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:47.880
injected at the closed end in this case

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:52.139
has a frequency 750 Hertz that is not

00:07:52.139 --> 00:07:55.400
aligned with a resonance

00:07:56.699 --> 00:07:59.099
a standing wave is not produced at this

00:07:59.099 --> 00:08:01.620
frequency rather the amplitude of the

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.740
input sound is highly attenuated as it

00:08:04.740 --> 00:08:08.180
propagates in the tube

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:14.240
thank you

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:16.919
the boundary condition of zero pressure

00:08:16.919 --> 00:08:20.520
at the open end of the tube is an

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:23.180
idealization

00:08:23.220 --> 00:08:25.379
in reality the section of air and

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:27.840
vibration at the lips transmits a small

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.120
amount of acoustic energy that radiates

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.000
outward away from the end of the tube

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.740
while typically far less than one

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.599
percent of the total energy produced

00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:38.820
during speech or singing

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.919
this is the sound that is actually heard

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:43.140
by a listener

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.360
this correction

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.760
also slightly increases the effective

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:50.459
length of the tube and results in a

00:08:50.459 --> 00:08:53.339
lowering of each resonance frequency as

00:08:53.339 --> 00:08:55.740
can be seen in the frequency response

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.100
function

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.959
standing waves corresponding to each of

00:09:06.959 --> 00:09:08.580
the first three resonances of the

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:11.220
uniform tube will be shown again but

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:15.019
with the correction for sound radiation

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.560
the patterns of pressure variation

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:27.540
appear to be nearly identical to those

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.640
in the idealized cases

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.140
the difference is simply that the

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.760
frequencies at which the standing waves

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:36.120
occur are slightly lower than before

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.339
note that in each case the upward and

00:09:38.339 --> 00:09:40.500
downward movement of the small black dot

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:42.620
at the right side of each pressure plot

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.880
indicates the radiated pressure

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.540
foreign

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.100
although the uniform tube is useful for

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:01.080
understanding the basic Acoustics of the

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.540
vocal tract it is not a realistic

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:05.459
configuration

00:10:05.459 --> 00:10:07.620
in these two cases the uniform tube will

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:09.720
morph into a tubular version of an e

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:11.279
vowel on the left

00:10:11.279 --> 00:10:14.220
and an ah vowel on the right both of

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.720
which were measured from a real person

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:19.500
using magnetic resonance imaging

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.959
as the vocal track shape changes the

00:10:21.959 --> 00:10:23.519
corresponding frequency response

00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:27.080
functions will also change

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.060
the deformation of the uniform tube into

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:47.120
realistic vocal tract configurations

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.680
shifts the resonance frequencies upward

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:52.320
or downward into a pattern that is

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:56.899
representative of each respective vowel

00:11:01.019 --> 00:11:03.120
standing waves will now be demonstrated

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.339
for the first three resonances of the

00:11:05.339 --> 00:11:08.959
vowels e and ah

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:14.940
the first Resonance of this particular e

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.899
vowel is 227 Hertz as can be seen

00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:20.700
however the standing wave associated

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.220
with this frequency is similar to the

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:25.260
standing wave observed for the first

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.540
Resonance of the uniform tube

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.180
which had a frequency of 500 Hertz

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.100
that is the pressure oscillates between

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.320
large positive and large negative values

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.600
in the back portion of the vocal tract

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.420
and tapers to nearly but not quite zero

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.779
at the lips the difference is that the

00:11:42.779 --> 00:11:44.940
pressure variation along the vocal tract

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:47.640
length is modified by the expansions and

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.320
constrictions that form the

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:52.220
e-configuration

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.240
the first Resonance of this particular

00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:01.680
ah vowel is 811 Hertz but again the

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.240
standing wave associated with this

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.519
frequency is similar to the standing

00:12:05.519 --> 00:12:07.920
wave observed for the first Resonance of

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:11.040
both the uniform tube and the E vowel

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.959
the pressure variation along the vocal

00:12:12.959 --> 00:12:15.420
tract length however is modified by the

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.640
constrictions and expansions that form

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:20.399
the ah configuration

00:12:20.399 --> 00:12:22.440
the standing waves for the second and

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.899
third resonances of the E and ah vowels

00:12:24.899 --> 00:12:28.880
will now be played consecutively

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:32.579
watch carefully for similarities in

00:12:32.579 --> 00:12:34.740
locations of zero pressure and

00:12:34.740 --> 00:12:37.380
differences of pressure amplitudes in

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:41.180
other regions of the vocal tract

00:13:08.839 --> 00:13:11.399
you may have observed that the locations

00:13:11.399 --> 00:13:13.740
of zero pressure or nodes is quite

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:15.720
similar for standing waves associated

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:18.000
with each resonance even though the

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.579
frequency of those resonances is quite

00:13:20.579 --> 00:13:23.160
different due to the specific vocal

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:26.040
tract configuration

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.740
as we produce speech or sing the shape

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.480
of the vocal tract undergoes almost

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:33.180
continuous change in order to shift the

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:35.339
frequencies at which standing waves will

00:13:35.339 --> 00:13:37.079
be supported

00:13:37.079 --> 00:13:39.180
this allows for easy passage of those

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:40.860
frequency components aligned with a

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.120
resonance

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:44.459
through the vocaltrex system and to the

00:13:44.459 --> 00:13:45.839
outside world

00:13:45.839 --> 00:13:47.700
the continual change in the frequency

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.980
bands that are enhanced or suppressed by

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:51.360
this process

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:54.540
is the means by which talkers encode a

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:56.700
message that is transmitted to a

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:59.060
listener

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.680
all of the examples shown thus far have

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.420
been based on a vocal tract length of

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.760
17.5 centimeters

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:11.399
as mentioned previously this is a

00:14:11.399 --> 00:14:13.500
typical length of an adult male vocal

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:14.880
tract

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.800
for comparison

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:18.600
a typical length of an adult female

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:20.700
vocal tract is about 15 and a half

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.980
centimeters whereas a two-year-old child

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.560
has a vocal tract that is about

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:29.300
10.5 centimeters long

00:14:29.339 --> 00:14:31.560
this animation shows the frequency

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:34.680
response function of the uniform tube as

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:37.139
the length is shortened from 17 and a

00:14:37.139 --> 00:14:40.940
half to ten and a half centimeters

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.440
as can be observed the shortening of

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.420
vocal tract length systematically

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.339
increases the frequency of each

00:14:53.339 --> 00:14:54.540
resonance

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.760
had shorter vocal tracts been used for

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:58.920
animating the standing waves at each

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:01.320
resonance frequency the patterns of

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:03.420
pressure variation along the vocal tract

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.180
would have appeared essentially the same

